# Environment
.env
# `make persist-env-secret` rewrites .env through `mktemp .env.XXXXXX`, and that
# temporary file holds a full copy including every secret until the mv lands. A
# trap removes it on failure, but a SIGKILL leaves it behind — and the server
# runs the deploy inside a git checkout, so an unignored copy would sit there.
.env.*
!.env.example

